  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ -3 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operations: \n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{3}{1+\\text{i}}{R}_{1}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ -3 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{3}{1+\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ -3+\\frac{3}{1+\\text{i}}\\cdot (1+\\text{i}) & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result  is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
